<div class="hero" style="min-height: auto; padding: 4rem 1rem 3rem;">
    <div class="hero-content" style="max-width: 1000px; width: 100%;">
        <h1 class="hero-title">Hey, I'm Trae.</h1>

        <div class="verse-box text-start" style="max-width: 100%;">
            <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #ddd;">
                I'm a cybersecurity graduate student, systems tinkerer, and the founder of
                England Technologies LLC, based out of the Jacksonville, Florida area.
            </p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                Most of my time is spent deep in Linux environments, building self-hosted network
                services, testing defensive infrastructure, and writing software to automate everyday
                workflows. Whether I'm managing server racks, dialing in a CoreXY 3D printer, or writing
                custom tools from scratch, I believe in understanding systems from bare metal up to the
                application layer, and in keeping critical services self-hosted, private, and open source
                whenever possible.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex gap-2 justify-content-center flex-wrap">
                <a class="btn btn-outline-info" style="color: var(--et-accent, #00bfff) !important;" href="/contact">Book Online</a>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-light" style="color: var(--et-btn-text, #e0e0e0) !important;" href="tel:+19042580217">Call 904-258-0217</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="container py-4">
    <h2 class="mb-2" style="color: #00bfff;">What I Do</h2>
    <p class="mb-3" style="color: #aaa;">
        I run my own home lab of firewalls, servers, and storage, set up the way a business would do it,
        so the fixes I bring to your computer and network are tested on real systems. I use Linux every
        day, and I'm comfortable working on Windows and macOS too.
    </p>
</section>

